# Ultra-Secure SSH Configuration for WPlib Remote Development
# Key-only auth, chrooted SFTP, hardened algorithm policy.
#
# The hardening directives live in sshd_config.d/hardening.conf (Included at
# the bottom) so they survive alongside host keys; only the bare minimum that
# must be set FIRST (privilege-drop user + host key paths) is here.
#
# Validated with `sshd -t`. Do NOT add options this OpenSSH build does not
# know (e.g. KerberosAuthentication / GSSAPIAuthentication on a no-Kerberos
# build) or algorithms it does not implement (e.g. ssh-ed448 in
# HostKeyAlgorithms) — sshd refuses to start on either mistake.

Port 2222
ListenAddress 0.0.0.0
Protocol 2

# Run unprivileged child sessions as the dev user.
UsePAM no

# Host keys are generated by /entrypoint.sh on first boot and persisted in
# the ssh_host_keys volume (mounted at /etc/ssh), so explicit HostKey lines
# are added there at startup. Fallbacks for images built without the volume:
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_rsa_key

# Hardening policy (auth, ciphers, MACs, KEX, chroot Match block).
Include /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/*.conf
